# =============================================================================
# RELATIONSHIP ARCHIVE — ROOT .gitignore
# Git repo root: D:\Relationship Chat Reconstruction Webpage\
#
# PURPOSE: Prevent accidental tracking of private source exports, generated
# datasets, credentials and build outputs. This file does NOT restrict what
# Antigravity (or any other tool) can read on disk — that is enforced by
# keeping originals outside the app bundle and by the AGENTS.md / SKILL.md
# access rules, not by Git.
#
# BEFORE COMMITTING: run  git status --short  and confirm that no private file
# appears as staged or tracked. If a private file was ever committed, it must
# be removed from history with  git filter-repo  or BFG before the repo is
# shared anywhere.
# =============================================================================


# =============================================================================
# 1. PRIVATE SOURCE EXPORTS (at repo root — never track originals)
# =============================================================================

# Original WhatsApp and Instagram exports and all their media
Messages Exports/

# Legacy or alternative export drop locations (guard against accidental drops)
exports/
source-exports/


# =============================================================================
# 2. SKILL PACKAGE — read-only; track as reference only if explicitly intended
# =============================================================================
# The skill folder is read-only. Its Python __pycache__ is build noise.
# If you DO want to track the skill package itself, remove the next block.
chatgpt_relationship-archive-reconstruction-v3.6/tools/__pycache__/
chatgpt_relationship-archive-reconstruction-v3.6/**/__pycache__/


# =============================================================================
# 3. GENERATED / PRIVATE DATA (inside relationship-archive/)
# =============================================================================

# Untouched export copies placed inside the app workspace
relationship-archive/data/source/

# Parsed and normalized event chunks (.jsonl) — contain full message text
relationship-archive/data/normalized/

# Original media bytes (copied from exports for the archive)
relationship-archive/data/media/

# Derived media: thumbnails, waveforms, transcripts (AI-generated derivatives)
# Actual subfolder on disk is "deprived-media" (typo preserved from scaffold)
relationship-archive/data/deprived-media/
# Also guard the canonical name in case it is corrected later
relationship-archive/data/derived-media/

# Search indexes (pre-computed search keys — regenerable from normalized data)
relationship-archive/data/indexes/

# Media manifests with hashes and private path metadata
relationship-archive/data/manifests/

# Public-facing bundle outputs that contain archive data
relationship-archive/public/archive-data/
relationship-archive/public/private-media/
relationship-archive/public/data/


# =============================================================================
# 4. LOCAL SECRETS AND ENVIRONMENT FILES
# =============================================================================

.env
.env.local
.env.development
.env.production
.env.staging
.env.test
# Allow a committed .env.example (no real values) if one is added later
!.env.example

# Any credentials, token, cookie or key files dropped locally
*.pem
*.key
*.pfx
*.p12
credentials.json
secrets.json


# =============================================================================
# 5. PYTHON CACHES AND VIRTUAL ENVIRONMENTS
# =============================================================================

__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.pyo
*.pyd
.Python
.venv/
venv/
env/
*.egg-info/
dist/
*.egg


# =============================================================================
# 6. NODE / JAVASCRIPT BUILD OUTPUTS AND CACHES
# =============================================================================

node_modules/
relationship-archive/node_modules/

# Build outputs
relationship-archive/dist/
relationship-archive/build/
relationship-archive/.next/
relationship-archive/out/
relationship-archive/.vite/
relationship-archive/.cache/

# Package manager lock files are intentionally NOT ignored — commit them
# (package-lock.json, yarn.lock, pnpm-lock.yaml carry exact dep versions)


# =============================================================================
# 7. OS AND EDITOR NOISE
# =============================================================================

# Windows
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
Desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/

# macOS
.DS_Store
.AppleDouble
.LSOverride
._*

# VS Code workspace state (keep .vscode/settings.json if you want shared config)
.vscode/.roaming
*.code-workspace

# JetBrains IDEs
.idea/

# Vim / Emacs swap files
*.swp
*.swo
*~
\#*\#


# =============================================================================
# 8. LOGS AND TEMPORARY FILES
# =============================================================================

# Antigravity task/session logs (Antigravity-internal; not project artifacts)
.gemini/

# Temporary parser outputs (atomic-write pattern writes .tmp before rename)
*.tmp

# General logs outside the project's structured log files
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*


# =============================================================================
# 9. WHAT IS INTENTIONALLY TRACKED
# =============================================================================
# The following are explicitly NOT ignored and should be committed:
#
#   relationship-archive/AGENTS.md           — project working principles
#   relationship-archive/PROJECT-STATUS.md   — human-readable project state
#   relationship-archive/README.md           — project README
#   relationship-archive/package.json        — dependency declarations
#   relationship-archive/docs/               — architecture, schema, plans
#   relationship-archive/logs/decisions.json — append-only decision log
#   relationship-archive/logs/operations.json— append-only operation log
#   relationship-archive/state/              — project-state.json + checkpoints
#   relationship-archive/project-manifest.json
#   relationship-archive/src/                — application source (future)
#   relationship-archive/tests/              — test code (future)
#   relationship-archive/scripts/            — ingestion scripts (future)
#   chatgpt_relationship-archive-reconstruction-v3.6/  (skill package, read-only)
#
# NOTE: data/manifests/media-manifest.json contains only hashes and relative
# paths — no message text or media bytes — so it MAY be committed if wanted.
# Decide deliberately before committing it.

